  `docs/security/pending-permissions.md`.

## Required experiment and state matrix

Start one app-server on a unique `/tmp` endpoint, attach the stock frontend with
`codex --remote <endpoint>` in a tmux pane, and connect a separate probe client.
Use the installed schema to perform initialization and thread discovery/resume;
do not hard-code a request shape copied from an older version.

Capture sanitized request/response/notification evidence for every cell:

- frontend connected, idle, composer empty;
- frontend connected, idle, composer contains an unsent distinctive draft;
- frontend connected, turn running;
- frontend disconnected while app-server remains temporarily reachable;
- app-server unavailable/restarted;
- authorized probe versus an unrelated same-UID process with no capability.

For each cell record whether `thread/inject_items` is accepted, where the item
appears (model history and/or TUI), whether any turn starts, whether the draft
changes, and which protocol notification or observable state distinguishes the
cell. Explicitly search the schema/event stream for a composer-empty/draft-
present signal. If none exists, record that absence as a blocker; visual tmux
observation is proof of preservation but is not a production composer signal.

Probe the control boundary by attempting, without the proposed credential or OS
capability, to connect and invoke at least `thread/inject_items`, `turn/start`,
`turn/steer`, `turn/interrupt`, and representative shell/filesystem-capable
methods exposed by the installed schema. Unix path obscurity and mode bits alone
do not count as same-UID isolation. Never point destructive probes at a real
user thread or workspace; use a disposable directory and harmless commands.

## Deliverables and receipt

- A fixture-gated probe/test that can be rerun against a future Codex version.
- A dated `.collab/research/` receipt containing: Codex version and binary path;
  exact launch/schema commands; endpoint and auth design; sanitized JSON-RPC
  request/response/notification excerpts; the completed state matrix; cleanup
  result; and separate `protocol`, `control_boundary`, and `composer_signal`
  verdicts.
- A final overall `GO`, `CONDITIONAL_GO`, or `NO_GO` decision. A conditional
  decision must name the exact prerequisite task/feature still required.
- No access tokens, full prompts, user drafts, home paths beyond what is needed
  to identify the binary, or version-generated schemas committed to git.

## Acceptance criteria

- The installed schema, not memory or web documentation alone, establishes the
  exact initialization, thread attach/resume, injection, and notification forms.
- A real tmux session proves remote TUI attach and passive injection across the
  entire state matrix, including a non-empty unsent composer draft.
- Evidence proves injection itself starts no turn and never calls
  `turn/start`, `turn/steer`, or `turn/interrupt`.
- The receipt identifies a production-usable composer-state signal, or clearly
  blocks automatic wake-on-message until one exists. No inference from process
  idleness or elapsed time counts as composer-empty proof.
- The receipt identifies and demonstrates an authenticated transport or true OS
  identity boundary. An unauthorized same-UID probe cannot exercise active
  controls. If this cannot be achieved with installed Codex, the verdict is
  `NO_GO` for T002/T003 rather than weakening the boundary.
- Injected message content remains a data item: the spike does not execute it,
  create an approval verdict, or make `await-reply` succeed.
- App-server and tmux processes/endpoints are removed at the end, including on
  probe failure.

## Verification commands

Record exact return codes in the receipt. At minimum run:

```sh
codex --version
codex --help
codex app-server --help
./scripts/c2c_tmux.py list
just build
just check
```

Also run the new focused fixture test and its documented tmux probe command.

## Blockers

None. This is the evidence-producing prerequisite. T002 and T003 remain blocked
unless the protocol and control-boundary verdicts are positive; any automatic
turn-wake work also remains blocked unless a reliable composer-state signal is
found or Codex gains one.
